// Base64-encoded Crimson Pro font files (SIL Open Font License), embedded
// directly as source constants -- NOT read from disk at runtime.
//
// Why embedded as data rather than read from a font file on disk: the
// print/PDF pipeline runs inside a Vercel serverless function on a
// stripped-down headless Chromium (@sparticuz/chromium) that does not
// ship the Georgia/Times New Roman fonts our CSS asked for, and (unlike
// this project's dev machines) apparently has no real serif font
// installed as a fallback either -- confirmed 2026-09-06 by inspecting a
// real exported PDF's embedded font resources directly: every character
// had silently been substituted with a generic sans-serif ("Open Sans"),
// which is why exported PDFs looked visibly different (lighter, airier,
// sans-serif) from a same-size Vellum-exported reference book despite
// having correct page size and margins. Embedding the actual font bytes
// in the generated HTML guarantees the intended typeface renders
// correctly regardless of what fonts (if any) the runtime happens to
// have installed -- this is also how Vellum and other real publishing
// tools guarantee consistent output.
//
// A plain fs.readFileSync() of a font file living in this package would
// have been simpler, but this project has already been burned once by
// Vercel's build-time file tracer missing a non-statically-referenced
// file read from node_modules at runtime (see the long comment at the
// top of render-pdf.ts about pagedjs's dist/ folder needing an explicit
// outputFileTracingIncludes entry) -- embedding the bytes as an actual
// imported module avoids that whole class of bug entirely, at the cost
// of a larger source file.
//
// Regenerating these constants (e.g. to update the font or add a
// weight): the source files come from the @fontsource/crimson-pro npm
// package (files/crimson-pro-latin-400-normal.woff2 etc.), base64-encoded.

export const CRIMSON_PRO_REGULAR =
  "";

export const CRIMSON_PRO_ITALIC =
  "";

export const CRIMSON_PRO_BOLD =
  "";

export const CRIMSON_PRO_BOLD_ITALIC =
  "";
